Package: ivppmlhdfe
Type: Package
Title: IV-PPML with High-Dimensional Fixed Effects
Version: 0.10.0
Date: 2026-11-19
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ohyun", "Kwon", email = "theekwonomist@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Mario", "Larch", role = "aut"),
    person("Jangsu", "Yoon", role = "aut"),
    person("Yoto V.", "Yotov", role = "aut"))
Description: Instrumental-variables Poisson pseudo-maximum likelihood (IV-PPML) with
    high-dimensional fixed effects. The additive moment E[q(y - mu)] = 0 is solved by
    iteratively reweighted two-stage least squares with the fixed effects concentrated out
    at each iteration. The fixed-effect engine eliminates the fixed effect with the most
    levels exactly and solves the rest by Jacobi-preconditioned conjugate gradients, with
    warm starts and a staged inner tolerance. Reproduces the conventions of the Stata
    command 'ivppmlhdfe' (singletons, separation, collinearity, robust and multi-way
    cluster standard errors, weights, offsets) and reports first-stage statistics.
    Pure R: no compiled code.
